1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,200
a² + b² = c². They teach you this at school. You're about to realise what for.

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:05,600
A screen. Any screen you own.

3
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:07,200
a is across.

4
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:08,800
b is up.

5
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:09,600
c is corner to corner.

6
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:13,600
Measure across: 8. Drag it into a.

7
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:18,400
Measure up: 6. Drag it into b. That is everything you can reach a ruler to.

8
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:21,600
8 squared is 64. 6 squared is 36.

9
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:25,600
64 plus 36 is 100. So c squared is 100 — and c is 10.

10
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:28,800
You never measured the diagonal. The equation handed it to you.

11
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:32,800
The box says 10 inches. Every screen is sold by its diagonal.

12
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:36,400
We learned this at school. Nobody ever said what for.

13
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:40,000
Pause. Observe. Learn. Follow for the math behind AI — @observer.collapse
